@17860 dr_block_exit
    A translated block ends with a call to this routine when the block that
    follows is at a fixed address: pc already holds that address (plus 2).
    Look it up; if a translation exists, dr_chain_block replaces the call
    that came here with a direct branch to it, otherwise translate it.
    (Also reached by falling out of the special event processing in
    dr_exit_to_interpreter.)

@10BEC dr_bcc_flags
    Record flags for a conditional branch, indexed by its condition (T, F,
    HI, LS, CC, CS, NE, EQ, VC, VS, PL, MI, GE, LT, GT, LE).  All are 0x2300,
    a control transfer that reads every flag.  The low bits sort the
    conditions into classes for the emitters: 0x20 for the six that test C
    and Z, 0x12 for the four signed comparisons.

@10DD0 dr_decode_addx_or_add
10DF0 DEFECT: ADDX also reads Z (it never sets it), so 0x100 belongs here too

@127C0 dr_emit_move_w
    Code generator for MOVE.W and MOVEA.W.
    .
    DEFECT IN THE ORIGINAL CODE.  A register-direct source is turned into a
    PowerPC register number by adding the opcode's low four bits to 8,
    which gives r8-r15 for D0-D7 and r16-r22 for A0-A6 - and r23 for A7,
    which actually lives in r1.  The path for a data register destination
    tests for A7 (dr_emit_move_w_L4 compares the four bits with 15) and
    handles it; the paths for a memory destination and for MOVEA.W do not.
    The 50 opcodes MOVE.W A7,<memory> and MOVEA.W A7,An are therefore
    translated into code that reads r23, the recompiler's own entry
    address, in place of the stack pointer.  Found by tools/fuzz.py.
